    {
      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle.\n2. Determine the supplement of the complement obtained in step 1.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle\nThe complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in 90 degrees. Therefore, we need to find the angle that, when added to 42 degrees, equals 90 degrees.\n\n\\[\n90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSo, the complement of a 42-degree angle is 48 degrees.\n\n### Step 2: Determine the supplement of the complement\nThe supplement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in 180 degrees. Therefore, we need to find the angle that, when added to 48 degrees, equals 180 degrees.\n\n\\[\n180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSo, the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is 132 degrees.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \\boxed{132}.",
